<p>{% trans %}Field settings control which name parts are active and how editors enter data.{% endtrans %}</p>

<h2>{% trans %}Main choices{% endtrans %}</h2>
<ul>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Components</strong>: Turn each name part on or off.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Minimum components</strong>: Choose which parts are required before save.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Allow family or given</strong>: Allow one of these to satisfy both required checks.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Field type</strong>: Use text, select, or autocomplete for each part.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Maximum length</strong>: Limit how many characters each part can store.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ul>

<h2>{% trans %}Options lists{% endtrans %}</h2>
<p>{% trans %}Title and generational fields can use option lists. Add one option per line. You can also import values from taxonomy terms when available.{% endtrans %}</p>

<h2>{% trans %}Blank prompt option{% endtrans %}</h2>
<p>{% trans %}You can show a prompt at the top of a select list. Start one line with <code>--</code> to set the prompt text.{% endtrans %}</p>
<ul>
  <li>{% trans %}<code>--Please select a title</code> shows "Please select a title" when nothing is chosen yet.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}The prompt is not a real value. Saving without choosing shows an empty field.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Without a <code>--</code> line, the list starts at the first real option with no prompt.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Use only one <code>--</code> line per option list.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ul>
